{
  "about": [
    "The adoption gate's rules as cases both clients run: the Mac (Tests/GuideAdoptionTests/AdoptionCasesTests.swift) and Windows (windows/Promptly.Guide.Core.Tests/AdoptionCasesTests.cs), so the two cannot drift apart without a test failing on one side.",
    "A category is written as the Mac stores it (AdoptionCategory.stored): \"<kind>:<id>\". Kinds and ids are the ones contracts/atlas-guide.json uses.",
    "bands: count out of total, and the band's text; null where the pair is not a share.",
    "categories: whether a stored category reads back (AdoptionCategory.restored). Only what a factory could have made does.",
    "reports: tallies through AdoptionGate.report with the kinds turned on. figures are sorted by team, then category. teams_too_small is for the gate's own checks and is never shown.",
    "refusals: AdoptionGate.refusal for one category of one tally; null when it is shown.",
    "contributions: what AdoptionConsent.contribution makes for an offer and an answer; null when nothing may be sent.",
    "tallies: contributions (each one person's month) combined into a team's tally for one month.",
    "last_finished: the latest month a contribution can be for, at a moment (UTC).",
    "intake: whether a month's contribution may be sent at a moment: from the end of the month until 00:00 UTC on the 7th of the month after (Atlas's INTAKE_CLOSES_ON_DAY). Both clients run these."
  ],
